<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1491"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nietzsche<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nietzsche<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, November 30, 2004 - 11:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I haven&#39;t researched BTK files in depth but here&#39;s my 2-&#39;sense&#39; anyway: <BR> <BR>I&#39;m somewhat of a poet and I don&#39;t believe BTK&#39;s poetry comes from a college-educated man. I don&#39;t believe his mistakes are purposeful and calculated. He tries to steer verse to rhyme and uses untried words in a way to make him sound pseudo-intelligent and educated. Furthermore, his punctuation is abysmal and he would have failed any college English class.  <BR> <BR>I think he respects education and is probably fairly frustrated he is not more accomplished. He seems to want to spend a lot of time at the library to augment this. <BR> <BR>A Xerox-trace proved BTK had Wichita State University library access when he was killing. But he used the City Library to relay a message. Why not WSU? <BR> <BR>My gut tells me this guy was not a student At WSU but more likely a Janitor or other non-teaching staff there during the mid-70&#39;s. <BR> <BR>Was this thoroughly investigated? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1491-->
<!--Post: 1498--><!--Time: 1101909119-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1498"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxtrotnem<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxtrotnem<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 01, 2004 - 5:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->they said he was a copier repair man, maybe he was working on a copier at wsu at the time he made the copy........possibly to test it out to see if it worked??????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
